  {
    "entity": 17592186124797,
    "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
    "identity": "q-158180",
    "issue": "validation",
    "message": "Unclosed TeX group or environment",
    "value": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>0 \\\\ y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y>0,\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$"
  },
  {
    "entity": 17592186278206,
    "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
    "identity": "q-158558",
    "issue": "validation",
    "message": "Unclosed TeX group or environment",
    "value": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-1\\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}x\\ge 1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge 1,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1}.\n$$"
  },
  {
    "entity": 17592186278207,
    "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
    "identity": "q-158560",
    "issue": "validation",
    "message": "Unclosed TeX group or environment",
    "value": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y\\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4>0\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}x\\ge y \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}.\n$$"
  },
  {
    "entity": 17592186278209,
    "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
    "identity": "q-158564",
    "issue": "validation",
    "message": "Unclosed TeX group or environment",
    "value": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2y\\ge 0 \\\\ 2-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2}.\n$$"
  },
  {
    "entity": 17592186378787,
    "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
    "identity": "q-158563",
    "issue": "validation",
    "message": "Unclosed TeX group or environment",
    "value": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero, and\n\n- the expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+2\\ge 0 \\\\ 2{x}^{3}-y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge -2 \\\\ y\\ne 2{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -2,\\,y\\ne 2{x}^{3}}.\n$$"
  },
  {
    "entity": 17592186378815,
    "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
    "identity": "q-158589",
    "issue": "validation",
    "message": "Unclosed TeX group or environment",
    "value": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The argument of the arccosine has values between $-1$ and $1,$ and\n\n- the expression under the square root must be non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-1<x+\\sqrt{y}<1 \\\\ y\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x+\\sqrt{y}\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0}.\n$$"
  }
